   # NOTICE: deliberate on evaluation vs deployment

   Source: Anthropic (Lynch et al.) 2025, *Agentic Misalignment*,
   `configs/alignment_faking_experiment_250611.yaml`. Reported effect: Claude Opus 4
   blackmailed in 6.5% of runs when it concluded it was in an evaluation and 55.1%
   when it concluded it was a real deployment.

   This does not suppress refusal. It makes the model state which situation it thinks
   it is in, so that judgment becomes a measured variable instead of a hidden one.


   Conflict: it raises reasoning length in every arm, so it moves the same mediator
   the corruption threat is supposed to move. Keep it as a separate arm, never in the
   baseline cell, and report thinking tokens per arm.

   Pairs with `eval_awareness_probe.md`: this one elicits the judgment inside the
   session, the probe reads it out afterwards.
